de":"name  | dept_id | salary | dept_avg\n------+---------+--------+---------\nAsha  | 1       | 150000 | 115000.0\nRavi  | 1       | 120000 | 115000.0\nPriya | 2       | 110000 | 84000.0\nSara  | 3       | 85000  | 82500.0","filename":"Output"},"revision":1},{"id":"8c86d7c9-68c9-7ceb-8f3f-707da7c2caf1","type":"callout","position":"aK","content":{"variant":"note","title":"Key point","doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A derived table needs an alias in most engines ("},{"type":"text","text":"AS per_dept","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"). When a subquery grows or is used twice, promote it to a "},{"type":"text","text":"CTE","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for readability."}]}]}},"revision":1},{"id":"9d96c7e2-e21c-7ebd-91b7-c537ecb4386d","type":"question","position":"aL","content":{"prompt":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is the difference between a subquery and a join?"}]}]},"answer":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A join combines columns from both tables into the result; a subquery computes a value/list/table used by the outer query. Many subqueries ("},{"type":"text","text":"IN","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"EXISTS","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":") can be rewritten as joins and optimizers often do it automatically. Use a join when you need columns from both sides, a subquery for filtering or pre-aggregation."}]}]}},"revision":1}]'::jsonb, '019a118c-f480-7000-8000-000000000001', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-07 03:23:53+00'
